From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] seatop_default: the floating modifier and a touch move windows

A touch goes to the client as touch whenever the client accepts it, so
holding the floating modifier (Super) and dragging with a finger did
nothing over most GTK and Qt windows; only a mouse or the touchpad
could move a floating window.  With the modifier held, take the
pointer-simulation path instead: the touch is the left button, and
handle_button starts the move (or a tiling drag) as for a mouse.

Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-07), against swayfx 0.6 (sway 1.12).
---
--- a/sway/input/seatop_default.c
+++ b/sway/input/seatop_default.c
@@ -665,7 +665,14 @@
 	double sx, sy;
 	node_at_coords(seat, seat->touch_x, seat->touch_y, &surface, &sx, &sy);
 
-	if (surface && wlr_surface_accepts_touch(surface, wlr_seat)) {
+	// With the floating modifier held, a touch acts as the pointer's left
+	// button, so it can move a floating window (or drag a tiled one) as the
+	// modifier and a mouse do, also over clients that accept touch.
+	struct wlr_keyboard *keyboard = wlr_seat_get_keyboard(wlr_seat);
+	bool mod_pressed = keyboard &&
+		(wlr_keyboard_get_modifiers(keyboard) & config->floating_mod);
+
+	if (surface && !mod_pressed && wlr_surface_accepts_touch(surface, wlr_seat)) {
 		if (seat_is_input_allowed(seat, surface)) {
 			cursor->simulating_pointer_from_touch = false;
 			seatop_begin_touch_down(seat, surface, event, sx, sy, lx, ly);
